        "original_id": "3c88bf1f-155e-52d2-8daa-68906a3577b7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Piet Norval, Wayne Ferreira, Emilio Sánchez, Kevin Ullyett\n- Events: 1992 Summer Olympics, 1988 Olympic Games, 2000 Stockholm Open\n- Topics: doubles tennis, Davis Cup, wheelchair tennis\n\nFacts:\n- Emilio Sánchez won three Grand Slam doubles titles and the men's doubles silver medal at the 1988 Olympic Games.\n- Piet Norval represented his native country in the doubles competition at the 1992 Summer Olympics in Barcelona, where he partnered Wayne Ferreira.\n- Piet Norval and Kevin Ullyett were the defending champions at the 2000 Stockholm Open doubles event, but they lost in the semifinals.\n- Emilio Sánchez captained his nation to Davis Cup success in 2008 after retiring as a player.\n- In 2012, Emilio Sánchez was a tournament director for two wheelchair tennis events.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
